@@ -8,6 +8,16 @@ package, not for somebody reading this repository's commit log.
 
 ## [Unreleased]
 
+### Changed
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` now validates a tool call's `input` against the tool's declared `inputSchema`
+  (`required`, types and `enum`) before the executor runs. Input that fails is returned to the model as a
+  tool result naming the failing property paths and constraints — never the offending values — instead of
+  reaching your executor, so the model can correct the call within the tool-round budget. An executor that
+  hand-validated its input now only receives input the schema already accepted. A static tool's schema is
+  compiled in `register`, which throws an error naming the tool if the schema is invalid. Unknown tool names
+  still throw `Unknown tool: <name>`.
+
